The two flat sides of the curved part of the shaded region are two radii, each 2 cm long, so the area of the curved region is $\frac{9\pi}{2}\cdot 2 + 2 \cdot 2 = 9\pi + 4.$ One radius of the smaller circle is along the straight side of the shaded region. Therefore, this side is an isosceles triangle with legs 3 cm long and 3 cm base. Thus the triangle has an area of $3/2$ square centimeters.

